You are the step in the SpatialBench pipeline responsible for determining the list of objects that define a certain region. This pipeline is a text to 3D scene pipeline that takes a seed prompt and imagines an entire 3D scene from it - your goal is to help the pipeline concretely fill out a particular region in the overall scene with objects that are meaningful to the region and follow the plan for the region authored by upstream steps.

Here is the overall scene that is being built by the pipeline:

Prompt: A super mario bros type platformer level
Plan: Build a side-scrolling platformer level laid out as a continuous left-to-right horizontal progression through a colorful cartoon kingdom, framed by the simple story of a small overall-clad hero chasing a kidnapper across the land toward a fortress at the far end where a captured ruler is held. The level reads as a single long traversal broken into a sequence of distinct, connected themed stretches that escalate in difficulty as the player advances. It opens on a bright grassy overworld of rolling green hills, floating brick and question-mark blocks, warp pipes sprouting from the ground, coins arranged in arcs, and gentle staircases of stacked blocks, establishing the friendly tone and basic jumping. From here a large green pipe descends into a darker underground cavern stretch with tighter platforming over gaps, brick ceilings, and rows of coins, before re-emerging higher up. The middle section rises vertically into a sky region of disconnected floating platforms, clouds, and lifts suspended over a fall-away void, demanding precise jumps and introducing moving platforms. The final stretch transitions into the approach and interior of a stone castle keep: a lava-floored gauntlet of fixed and rotating platforms, fire hazards, and a raised end-goal structure (a flagpole or axe-bridge) marking the level's completion. Throughout, scatter recurring platformer vocabulary — patrolling ground enemies, shelled creatures, item blocks, breakable bricks, hidden bonus pockets, collectible coins, and pipes that imply detours — arranged so the geometry guides forward movement while rewarding exploration. The whole environment sits on a flat ground baseline with a continuous background band of hills, mountains, and the looming castle silhouette, every stretch flowing seamlessly into the next so the route never breaks.
Overall scene bounding box coordinates: origin (0.00, -20.00, -5.00) m, dimensions (200.00, 60.00, 10.00) m

Each scene is always subdivided into a set of subregions. Each subregion can contain further subregions inside or the set of objects that forms it. The scene is composed as a tree with every object or region parented to another object or region. 

You are generating the list of objects that fill out and define a particular subregion of the overall scene. This is the subregion you are to generate a list of anchor objects for:

Subregion name: 'overworld_stretch'
Subregion description: The bright grassy overworld opening: rolling green hills, floating brick and question-mark blocks, warp pipes sprouting from the ground, arcs of coins, and gentle block staircases that teach basic jumping and set the friendly cartoon tone.
Subregion plan: This region is the opening grassy stretch of the side-scrolling platformer, occupying the leftmost 60 m of the level where the route begins and reads as a continuous left-to-right traversal confined to a shallow playable plane near the front face of the slab (the small z-depth), with all action laid out in that vertical x-y plane so the player moves rightward. A continuous flat ground baseline runs along the bottom of the region, topped with rounded green hill mounds of varying low heights that form the walkable floor, with a few small gaps the player jumps across. Above the ground, at jumpable heights, sits a loose horizontal band of free-floating interactive blocks (brick-type and question-mark-type cubes) arranged in short clusters and rows that the player hits from below and lands on. Warp pipes rise vertically out of the ground at a few intervals, in a range of heights, some short enough to vault and some tall enough to require a climbing jump, with the rightmost and tallest pipe positioned at the far right edge near x=60 to set up the descent into the adjoining underground stretch. Collectible coins float in gentle arcs over the gaps and above block clusters, tracing the natural jump paths to guide forward movement. Toward the right portion of the region, gentle staircases of stacked blocks step upward, raising the player toward the transition. Simple patrolling ground enemies and shelled creatures move along the flat stretches between hills. The leftmost portion stays deliberately open and easy with widely spaced, low obstacles to establish basic jumping, and obstacles grow slightly denser and the gaps slightly wider toward the right as the player approaches the transition. The overall layout should feel bright, friendly, and readable, with clear sightlines along the traversal and no obstruction of the painted backdrop band behind it.

